  "rationale": "With no controls deployed, exfiltration is reachable. Phishing gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. With no segmentation, pivot_internal gives reach_internal. auth_appserver leads to kerberoast_dc, which gives stolen_admin. Then auth_dc, escalate_dc and dump_dbadmin_dc give stolen_dbadmin. Finally auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db complete the attack. So at least 1 control is needed. Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. The only techniques that give those footholds are auth_dc and auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. With mfa_admin true, stolen_dbadmin can never be obtained. That blocks every auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup technique, so no db, fileserver or backup foothold or admin is possible, and no exfiltrate technique can fire. Minimum = 1."
